  "reading": "A minor 2nd is NOT below the noise floor: its latent move is ~94% of a fifth's (magnitude SATURATES \u2014 displacement can't read interval SIZE), it is detectable (in-sample), and its melody-subspace share (0.096) beats codec hiss (0.080) and random (0.059). BUT the melody-subspace SNR over codec noise is only ~1.2x \u2014 the subspace the #59 loss boosts is barely more melodic than noisy, so upweighting it amplifies codec hiss almost as much as melody."
